'' TKO0871, fbc's 24 (T27): a 'print' item of a type with no printable form is refused
'' whatever shape the value takes -- a constructor call 'Box( 7 )', 'type<T>( ... )', a
'' dereference, an array element, a field, an 'iif', a function result. tiko refused a
'' variable and a function result but not a constructor call, an element or an 'iif':
'' those compiled, and the item that could not be lowered took the rest of the
'' statement with it -- 'print "X["; Box( 7 ); "]Y"' printed 'X[' and no newline. The
'' last line -- a zstring element, a number element, a numeric iif -- still prints.
'' Lines identical to fbc-modern's errors. See Unprintable_ in symbols/latesweeps4.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/print-unprintable-temp.bas
